# What the AeroBO desktop app needs at run time — the LEAN set, at the
# versions this shell was actually developed and tested against.
#
# NOT pyproject's dependency list. That list is the research environment
# (streamlit for the V1 shell, smt for multi-fidelity, pandas underneath
# streamlit) and costs ~285 MB the V4 app never imports: `streamlit` is
# reached by gui/app.py alone, and `smt` only by optimize/mf.py, which
# nothing in api.py or the shell calls.
#
# WHY EXACT PINS. The shell reaches into NiceGUI internals — v4/app.py's
# _only_the_root_page_is_a_page() replaces `nicegui.app.exception_handlers`
# 404 entry — so a minor bump is a real risk, not a theoretical one. A user
# downloading this in a year gets the stack the screenshots were taken on.
#
# WHY TWO FILES. The BO stack (torch) is locked separately in
# requirements-bo.in because it is the ONLY part that a supported machine
# can fail to install: PyTorch has published no macOS x86_64 wheel since
# 2.2.2, and its arm64 wheel is tagged macosx_14_0, so an Intel Mac and a
# Mac on Ventura or older both have nowhere to get it. api.py imports
# `optimize.bo` inside the function that runs it, so the shell starts fine
# without it and every non-BO optimiser (GA, SLSQP, DOE, penalty) works.
# The launcher installs this file first and MUST succeed; it installs the
# BO file second and, if that fails, says so and carries on.
#
# Compile with installer/lock.sh, never by hand.

nicegui==3.14.0           # the shell itself; 3.x page/router API
plotly==6.9.0             # every chart in stages 4 and 7
numpy==2.4.6
scipy==1.17.1             # LLT/VLM linear solves, SLSQP
matplotlib==3.11.0        # optimize/metrics.py's convergence plot (lazy)
pymoo==0.6.2              # the GA baseline

# The BO stack is NOT here — see requirements-bo.in.

# native window (macOS/Windows). Linux runs in the browser: pywebview needs
# GTK/WebKit system packages there that we cannot install for the user.
pywebview==6.2.1 ; sys_platform != 'linux'
